# Vue

- Follow `<script>` declarations and repository JavaScript or TypeScript configuration selected by the root guidance.
- Follow the installed Vue version, framework, and existing Options or Composition API style. Use `<script setup>` for new compatible components when it matches project policy; do not mechanically rewrite stable components.
- Use `ref`, `reactive`, and `computed` according to actual reactivity and identity needs; avoid destructuring that loses reactivity.
- Keep props read-only and emit explicit events. Use the repository's established state management for shared state.
- Preserve Single-File Component section boundaries, accessibility, and server/client behavior. Use configured Vue lint, formatter, and test tooling.
